cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "peptide-rpes: RPES peptide-rank scoring and a peptide-representation benchmark"
abstract: "Reproduction package for a methods/resource paper on RPES (Rank-Percentile Ensemble Score), a ceiling-effect-free rank-aggregation score for short food-derived peptides, and a head-to-head benchmark of physicochemical descriptors, a PCA latent space, and ESM-2 embeddings for the task of predicting RPES. RPES is a transparent aggregation module derived from physicochemical descriptors; it is not a bioactivity predictor, and no external activity label enters its construction. v1.1.0 adds a matched-initialisation ablation showing that the iterative search loop contributes exactly zero gain, corrects the no-loop control (0.8000 to 0.7282 on the library scoring scale), and adds the labelled training set required for full reproduction."
authors:
